#X text 261 309 These 3 messages control the excution of the unstet
process. The play message is applied imeadately \, the stop and pause
is applied only at the the of a period. Normaly these messages are
not needed \, as the unstat process starts playing automatically. You
can prevent this by starting the process as "unstet -n".;
#X text 25 646 bang;
#X text 225 650 periodend;
#X text 300 647 zuklusend;
#X text 408 647 playstart;
#X text 482 648 playstop;
#X text 653 722 rawbang;
#X text 456 500 When Pd and unstet run on the same computer \, these
messages are not needed \, as the defaults are ok. When they are on
different computers \, replace *localhost" with the IP of the computer
running unstet and send the connect message.;
#X text 645 740 (i.e. bangs w/o ornaments);
#X text 61 57 The unstet-abraction receives (several) bangs form a
running unstet process \, and can optionaly alter the process parameters
or can control the execution of the process. The unstet process should
be startet bevor the Pd process with the command "unstet".;
#X text 24 15 [unstet-abstraction]- integrates external unstet process
;
#X msg 76 222 variation 0 0 0 0 800 1600 2400 4000;
#X msg 123 273 teiler 2 3 5 8 13;
#X msg 29 171 periode 5000 5000 13000;
#X text 508 55 The messages "periode" \, "variation" and "teiler" alter
the default parameters in a unstet process. When your happy with the
defaults there is no need to use these messages. You can use these
messages anytime \, but the changes are applied only at the end of
a period.;
#X text 279 280 The "teiler" can any have length.;
